    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d468">

                <pb facs="0599" n="591" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760F.62/877: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-18T12:00:00+01:00">September 18,
                        1938—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received September 18—9:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>252. …</p>
                <p>Discussing the Jewish aspect of racial policy Mussolini declared<anchor n="35"
                        xml:id="d468-f1"/> the regime’s policy had been determined by the
                    irreconcilable hostility of international Jewry toward Fascism during the past
                    16 years despite the regime’s tolerance. Italian Jews who had undisputed <pb
                        facs="0600" n="592" xml:id="pg592"/> civil and military merits vis-à-vis
                    Italy and the regime would encounter understanding and justice; to the others
                    would be applied a policy of separation. The world would ultimately have to
                    admire the firmness and generosity of Italian policy unless the Jews at home and
                    abroad and their many unexpected friends forced a sudden revision.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d468-f1" n="35" xml:id="d468-f1-content">
                <p>Speech of September 18, 1938, at Trieste on the international situation.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
